course: dictionary
lesson: 7369
title: A word from ancient Rome
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Plebeian is a word about class and ordinary people. In ancient Rome, a plebeian was an ordinary citizen, not one of the rich noble families called patricians. «Rich old families were patricians and ordinary citizens were plebeians» tells you which group each person belonged to.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence: «the plebeians went on strike by leaving the city until they won more rights.» Ordinary citizens had fewer rights, so they fought for them. Ask yourself what word would fit: here, plebeian means one of the ordinary people, not one of the rich families.
explain: Outside history, plebeian can mean common or not refined, and some people use it to look down on others. Be careful with the short form «pleb». It is a rude insult in UK slang, and calling someone it is unkind, so do not use it, even if you hear others say it.
fact: Plebeian is a noun (a plebeian, plebeians) and an adjective (plebeian).
fact: «Plebeian» means an ordinary citizen of ancient Rome, not one of the rich noble families called patricians.
fact: Plebeian can also mean common, ordinary or not refined, and snobs often use it to look down on people or things.
fact: «Pleb» is a rude UK slang insult for someone thought to be common or low class; it is unkind, so do not use it to hurt anyone.
fact: Phrases you may meet: plebeians and patricians, plebeian tastes.
exercise: «Rich old families were patricians and ordinary citizens were plebeians.» In this sentence, what is a plebeian? | A rich noble from an old family | A type of Roman building | A soldier who fights on horses | *An ordinary citizen of ancient Rome
exercise: A snob says a film's style is plebeian. What does the snob suggest? | Ancient and written in Latin | *Common and not refined | Very expensive and grand | Brand new and very clever
exercise: What were the rich noble families of Rome called? | Plebeians | *Patricians | Tribes | Citizens
test: Why did the plebeians leave the city in the Rome sentence? | To find a new king | *To win more rights | To go on holiday | To build a wall
test: What is the most respectful thing to do with the word «pleb»? | Say it to show you are clever | Say it when a classmate is cross with you | Use it as a joke about a friend | *Leave it out, because it is an unkind insult
exam: Which two meanings does plebeian have? | A rich noble from an old family, and a type of horse | A Roman soldier, and a Roman god | *An ordinary Roman citizen, and common or not refined | A word for a fancy dress party
